Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 13:31:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/57] vulkan: add GGML_VK_FLOPS_PER_SUBMIT env override for
 submit granularity

Diagnostic knob for latency-bound decode on unified-memory iGPUs.
Neutral by default (keeps the flops/40 heuristic).

Measured on Strix Halo (gfx1151, 20 CU, Qwen3.8-Flash-Next 125B-A6B):
  default                          31.72 t/s
  FLOPS_PER_SUBMIT=0               31.41 t/s
  FLOPS=0 + MAX_NODES=100000       27.64 t/s
  MAX_NODES=100000                 31.10 t/s
=> the default heuristic is optimal; submit count is NOT the decode bottleneck.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
index 49241140cfb..8097374ba50 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
@@ -17887,6 +17887,17 @@ static ggml_status ggml_backend_vk_graph_compute(ggml_backend_t backend, ggml_cg
     }
     uint64_t flops_per_submit = std::min(flops_cap, ctx->last_total_flops / 40u);
 
+    // [TAG_SUBMIT_TUNE] override the submit granularity for latency-bound decode.
+    // GGML_VK_FLOPS_PER_SUBMIT=0 disables intra-graph flushes entirely (one submit per graph).
+    // Rationale: on unified-memory iGPUs the decode graph is latency-bound, not compute-bound;
+    // the default heuristic (total_flops/40) forces ~40 submits per token for no benefit.
+    {
+        static const char * e = getenv("GGML_VK_FLOPS_PER_SUBMIT");
+        if (e) {
+            flops_per_submit = strtoull(e, nullptr, 10);
+        }
+    }
+
     auto const submit_after = [&](int start, int end) {
         if (ctx->device->serialize_submissions) {
             try {
